","change":"Bettles has warmed, days and nights alike","rain":"Bettles has gotten wetter"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 23\u00b0F was the 15th warmest November 13 high of 82 since 1945, the warmest since 2016.","t_yest":"November 13: warmer than 83% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>23\u00b0F</strong> was the 15th warmest November 13 high of 82 since 1945, the warmest since 2016. The normal high for the date is 7\u00b0F, and the record is 45\u00b0F (1976). The low of <strong>20\u00b0F</strong> was the 3rd warmest November 13 low of 83 since 1944.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Bettles' climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Bettles has set <strong>73 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 119 that chance alone would give, and <strong>140 record highs</strong>, close to the 119 that chance alone would give. The 1990s hold the most record highs of any decade (69). Bettles' all-time high is 93\u00b0F, on July 6, 1986.","t_chg":"Bettles has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 81 complete years: Bettles' average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.40\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.19 to +0.60), about +3.2\u00b0F since 1945. Bettles' average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.69\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.49 to +0.87), about +5.5\u00b0F since 1945.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 4 of 12 months. Highs rose in 8 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Bettles has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Bettles' yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.56 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.23 to +0.89), about +4.5 inches since 1945. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 16.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 1965 (24.46 in); the driest, 1969 (6.88 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 1 daily record high, 1 daily record low"}}